  "description": "Standoff alignment records between the SBLGNT and the Berean Standard Bible for John 3:16, keyed to token ids, one record per correspondence: one-to-one, many-to-many (Οὕτως γὰρ with For … so; τὸν μονογενῆ with one and only), two explicit nulls (the articles ὁ and τὸν), one record of synthetic auto: origin with a confidence, and one English word (His) in no record at all, which is unaligned rather than null. The tokenization hashes are the SHA-256 of the `<token id>\\t<surface>\\n` lines of each token layer in id order; the stale case checks that a changed hash on either side invalidates the set. The apparatus siglum ⸀ before υἱὸν in the SBLGNT source file is not part of the text and is removed.",
